fix:
For a genuine plain data record with no invariants and no compatibility barrier, make the fields public or construct the struct directly instead of maintaining trivial accessor pairs. Where the object should own operations or hide its representation, move those operations into meaningful domain methods ("Tell, Don't Ask") and remove the raw manipulation API; do not fix representation leakage by blindly making domain state public.
```rust
pub struct EngineConfig {
    timeout: std::time::Duration,
    retries: u32,
}

impl EngineConfig {
    pub fn apply_to_request(&self, req: &mut Request) {
        req.set_timeout(self.timeout);
        req.set_retries(self.retries);
    }
}
